  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "trance: four on the floor with the bass on every offbeat eighth between the kicks, open hats on the same offbeats, a clap on two and four",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "One bar: the kick on the beats and the bass answering it on each and — the bounce every trance record from the late nineties rides — the root for three and the fifth under it for the last. A path cannot open on a rest, so each bar starts with a ghost of the root under the kick, a tenth of the weight and a tenth of a beat long. Open hats double the bass offbeats, closed sixteenths are left out. 136-140 is above the fast band's top (130), so it plays at 130 under the Techno key: trance has no key of its own yet."
  }
